; Made from the stand-in PlayStation 2 AV lead (ps2_av_cable.tscn), offered beside it
; on a card whose console names the "ps2_av_multi" socket (a mod's). Its plug:
;
; The plug is a box of Sony's measurements: the moulded body, 21.7 x 11.4 mm and
; 37.2 mm long, outside the case, and the metal shell that runs 7 mm into the
; socket along the plug's +Z. The origin is the body's front face, which is the
; frame a mod's socket seats a plug in. The collision box is the body only.
;
; The console end is a SHARED end carrying all five cords -- see CompositeCable.
; A COMPONENT lead (2026-11-21): the PlayStation 2's own Multi Out at the console, FIVE phonos
; at the set. The Multi Out's cords 0-4 are Y, L, R, Pb, Pr (MultiAvPort.CORD_CHANNELS),
; so cord_colors is in that order: green Y, white L, red R, blue Pb, red Pr; a real
; lead carries two reds too, and only the socket each lands in says which is which.
; Everything else is the composite lead's scene this was made from, two plugs more.
; collision_radius is the five-cord ribbon's half-width: 3 mm x 4 gaps / 2 + 1.5 mm.
[node name="Ps2ComponentCable" type="Node3D"]
script = ExtResource("1_cablescript")
cord_colors = PackedColorArray(0.16, 0.55, 0.24, 1, 0.87, 0.87, 0.84, 1, 0.72, 0.08, 0.08, 1, 0.14, 0.3, 0.68, 1, 0.72, 0.08, 0.08, 1)
wire_color = Color(0.07, 0.07, 0.075, 1.0)


